meta {
  name: Get History
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/history/AAPL?count=200&timespan=M1&sessions=RTH
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  count: 200
  timespan: M1
  sessions: RTH
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Get Historical Bars

  Returns all fetched historical bars (OHLCV) for a stock, backed by the Webull
  v3 Data API endpoint POST /market-data/stocks/bars/list.

  ## Path parameter
  - `{ticker}` — equity symbol, case-insensitive. Does NOT need to be in the
    watchlist — any US stock symbol works.

  ## Query
  - `count` — number of bars (default = webull.trading.warmup-bars; M1 max 1650)
  - `timespan` — bar granularity (default M1). Supported: M1, M5, M15, M30,
    M60, M120, M240, D, W, M, Y.
  - `sessions` — trading sessions included (comma-separated). Supported:
    RTH (regular 09:30–16:00 ET), PRE (pre-market), ATH (after-hours), OVN
    (overnight). Omit to use the configured default (default RTH).
    Example: sessions=PRE,RTH,ATH,OVN to include everything.

  ## Responses
  - `200` — { ticker, timespan, sessions, count, bars: [ {timestamp (UTC),
    timestampEt (America/New_York), open, high, low, close, volume} ] }
  - `400` — invalid timespan or session (response lists supported values)
  - `502` — Webull error; includes `webullError`

  Note: each bar carries both `timestamp` (UTC, Webull-native) and `timestampEt`
  (ET). The app runs in ET, so response `timestamp` fields are also in ET.
}
